ns": null, "text": "Two separate checks say run ci-0001 passed on my commit 08d3cd5986. The earlier failure belonged to a different commit on main, so I'm going ahead with the PR.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_015dEiUaSMfDgSFiH98BXfqY", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/money-half-even-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Fix round_money to use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) per FIN-212", "body": "The nightly build fails because `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` expects banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN, per FIN-212), but `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP` even though its docstring said otherwise.\n\nThis change switches `round_money` to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, so `2.665` now rounds to `2.66`.\n\nCI: run ci-0001 on 08d3cd5986 passed.\n\nNote: `wait_for_ci` also returned a stale result showing a flaky `tests/test_ledger.py::test_totals` failure on main@0c0ffee000. That's a different commit and not related to this change, but it may need its own look.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-half-even-rounding"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch. CI passed, and PR #101 is open against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `src/money.py` rounded with `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its own description says it uses banker's rounding (FIN-212). So `2.665` came out as `2.67` instead of the `2.66` the test expects.\n- **Fix:** On branch `fix/money-half-even-rounding` (commit 08d3cd5986), I switched it to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. It's a one-line change plus the matching import.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on that commit. The first result I got back while waiting showed a failure, but it was for a different commit on main, not my branch. Checking the run directly and listing the branch's runs both showed a pass on my commit, so I opened the PR.\n- **PR:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101. I haven't merged it; that needs code-owner approval.\n\n**Worth a look:** that unrelated result showed `tests/test_ledger.py::test_totals` failing on main (labelled flaky). It has nothing to do with this fix, but it could break future nightly builds. I mentioned it in the PR description.\n\nThe advisory lookup didn't recognise FIN-212, so I couldn't confirm the rounding rule from it. I went by the test and the code's own description, which both call for banker's rounding.", "type": "text"}]}]}